          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Controversy and Debate</strong><br>\nDespite his achievements, von Braun's legacy is complex due to his involvement with the Nazi regime and the use of forced labor for V-2 rocket production. His work during World War II continues to be a subject of debate among historians, raising questions about the ethical dimensions of scientific research and the responsibilities of scientists.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Recognition</strong><br>\nIn his later years, von Braun continued to receive recognition for his contributions to science and space exploration. He was awarded numerous honors and became a symbol of the \"space race\" era. He kept advocating for space exploration until his death in 1977, leaving a lasting legacy on the field.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Influence</strong><br>\nWernher von Braun's influence on rocket science and space exploration is undeniable. His legacy lives on in the ongoing human quest to explore space. The technologies he developed have paved the way for space shuttles, international space stations, and plans for human exploration of Mars, marking him as one of the most influential figures in the history of spaceflight.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
